    <item>
      <title>In search of connections that don't break</title>
      <link>https://journal.lu/en/search-connections-dont-break</link>
      <description>A single outage can cut people off from vital services, leaving them isolated in an interconnected world. Responses vary: some are grassroots and decentralised, built by communities; others are engineered, high-tech systems operated by companies or governments. Both provide resilience – and they distribute control in different ways.</description>
